    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d149">

                <pb facs="0248" n="142" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg142"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 U.S.S.R./115: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-09-08T15:00:00-04:00">September 8,
                            1934—3 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>235. Your 291, September 8. There is grave difficulty in fact that Congress when
                    considering Johnson bill was assured there would <pb facs="0249" n="143"
                        xml:id="pg143"/> be no credit transactions in advance of debt agreement
                    satisfactory to the President. Nothing said to Troyanovsky on any subject since conversation Wednesday
                        night<anchor n="64" xml:id="d149-f1"/> and it is up to him to take the next
                    step.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
